description: A formula keeps its casts, and a move keeps call order
globs: packages/engine/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Behavior

A numeric step keeps the casts in `docs/dev/engine/`: `s16`, `ftol`, `f32`. A truncating store and a final `f32` stay.

A move keeps the same calls and the same `await` order. One `try` / `finally` stays one `try` / `finally`.

After a change in this package, `npm test` and `npm run check` pass.

A mismatch with the notes goes in `docs/dev/engine/refactor-findings.md`: the effect, in English, with no quoted line and no script. The code keeps the behavior it had. Create that file only when there is a finding.

```ts
// Wrong: the product is rounded before the compare.
return f32((px - ax) * slope) <= py - ay;

// Right: pointBelowLine compares the product unrounded.
return (px - ax) * slope <= py - ay;
```
